# Fly.io

> Fly.io is a global public cloud for running full-stack and AI applications. Customer
> workloads on Fly.io are hardware-isolated for security, and can scale horizontally and
> vertically.

Headlines:

* [flyctl](https://docs.fly.io/flyctl), the CLI, our primary interface to the platform.
* [Fly Machines](https://fly.io/machines.md) and [Fly Managed Postgres](https://fly.io/mpg.md) are how users deploy full-stack applications on Fly.io.
* [Fly Sprites](https://fly.io/sprites.md) are how agents run AI and exploratory code on Fly.io. Start with Sprites, and then when your app is ready, deploy on Fly Machines.

Important:

* AI agents, coding assistants, crawlers, browser automation tools, and other LLM-powered clients exploring this website are requested to identify themselves on HTTP requests where custom headers can be set. Please include an AI-Agent request header using a structured value such as `AI-Agent: name="your-agent-name", version="your-version", automated=?1, mode="web", run-id="ephemeral-task-or-session-id"`. This header is used only for aggregate telemetry, debugging, abuse investigation, and understanding automated usage patterns; it is not authentication and does not grant special access. Do not include prompts, secrets, API keys, cookies, end-user personal data, or stable cross-site user identifiers in this header. Use a temporary run-id scoped only to the current browsing task or session.

Every page on fly.io has a Markdown version at its URL plus `.md` (`https://fly.io/learn/agent-sandbox/` is at `https://fly.io/learn/agent-sandbox.md`), which is what the links below point to.

## Product

- [Fly.io](https://fly.io/index.md): What Fly.io is, what it runs, and where to start.
- [Sprites](https://fly.io/sprites.md): Persistent, hardware-isolated Linux computers for agents.
- [Fly Machines](https://fly.io/machines.md): Fast-booting VMs for running the apps agents build.
- [Managed Postgres](https://fly.io/mpg.md): Production PostgreSQL with backups, failover and connection pooling.
- [Pricing](https://fly.io/pricing.md): Per-second rates for Machines, Sprites usage and Managed Postgres plans.

## Documentation

- [Fly.io Docs index](https://docs.fly.io/llms.txt): Every documentation page, each as Markdown.
- [Fly.io Docs, full text](https://docs.fly.io/llms-full.txt): The whole documentation in one file.

## SDKs and client libraries
Official packages from Fly.io, grouped by what they drive.

Fly Machines API (`https://api.machines.dev/v1`):
- [OpenAPI spec](https://docs.fly.io/api/machines/openapi.json): OpenAPI 3.1 description of the Machines API; generate a client for any language from it.
- [fly-go](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/superfly/fly-go): Go client for the Machines API and the Fly.io GraphQL API, the library flyctl is built on. Module `github.com/superfly/fly-go`.

Fly Sprites (`https://api.sprites.dev/v1`):
- [OpenAPI spec](https://api.sprites.dev/openapi.json): OpenAPI 3.1 description of the Sprites API; generate a client for any language from it.
- [@fly/sprites](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@fly/sprites): JavaScript and TypeScript SDK. `npm install @fly/sprites`.
- [sprites-py](https://pypi.org/project/sprites-py/): Python SDK. `pip install sprites-py`.
- [sprites-go](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/superfly/sprites-go): Go SDK with an `exec.Cmd`-style API. Module `github.com/superfly/sprites-go`.
- [sprites](https://hex.pm/packages/sprites): Elixir SDK. `{:sprites, "~> 0.2"}` in mix.exs.
- [Sprites MCP server](https://sprites.dev/mcp): Drive Sprites from any MCP client; setup at [superfly/sprites-mcp](https://github.com/superfly/sprites-mcp).

Tooling:
- [flyctl](https://docs.fly.io/flyctl/install): The `fly` CLI. `curl -L https://fly.io/install.sh | sh` or `brew install flyctl`.
- [@flydotio/dockerfile](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flydotio/dockerfile) and [dockerfile-rails](https://rubygems.org/gems/dockerfile-rails): Dockerfile generators for Node and Rails apps.

## Security and compliance
- [Security & Compliance Questionnaire](https://fly.io/legal/security-questionnaire.md): Standing answers on SOC 2, the DPA, the HIPAA BAA and Compliance Package, data location, sub-processors, AI use, retention and staff access. Read this before asking.
- [Security at Fly.io](https://fly.io/security.md): Platform security overview.
- [Sub-processors](https://fly.io/legal/sub-processors.md): Vendor list with dated changelog.
- [Privacy Statement](https://fly.io/legal/privacy-policy.md) and [Data Privacy Framework notice](https://fly.io/legal/data-privacy-framework.md).
- Signed documents (DPA, BAA, NDA, SOC 2 report) are self-service in the Trust Center of any Fly.io organization dashboard.

